    "q-100221": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100221",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${(18\\times \\frac{1}{3})}^{2}÷(2+{0.03}^{0}\\,)-3=$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nNotice that ${0.03}^{0}=1.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(18\\times \\frac{1}{3})}^{2}÷(2+{0.03}^{0}\\,)-3 & = \\\\ {(18\\times \\frac{1}{3})}^{2}÷(2+1\\,)-3 & = \\\\ {6}^{2}÷(2+1\\,)-3 & = \\\\ {6}^{2}÷3-3 & = \\\\ 36÷3-3 & = \\\\ 12-3 & = \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
