      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$((-4)^{0}-5)÷{2}^{2}+7=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. \n\nNotice that $(-4)^{0}=1.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((-4)^{0}-5)÷{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ (1-5)÷{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ -4÷{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ -4÷4+7 & = \\\\ -1+7 & = \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
