      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${8}^{0}+{2}^{3}\\times 4=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nNotice that ${8}^{0}=1.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{0}+{2}^{3}\\times 4 & = \\\\ 1+8\\times 4 & = \\\\ 1+(8\\times 4) & = \\\\ 1+32 & = \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}\n$$",
