    "q-100293": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100293",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${7}^{-1}\\times (2+\\frac{1}{3})=$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nNotice that ${7}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{-1}\\times (2+\\frac{1}{3}) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\times (2+\\frac{1}{3}) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\times \\frac{6+1}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\times \\frac{7}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times 7}{7\\times 3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times \\cancel{7}}{3\\times \\cancel{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
