    "q-100301": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100301",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Calculate ${(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}-11\\times {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, notice that\n$\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16}$\nis not zero. Any non-zero number raised to the power of $0$ equals $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n{(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the negative exponent and get\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3}={(\\frac{2}{1})}^{3}={2}^{3}=8.\n$$\n\nSubstituting all these values into the expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}-11\\times {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3} & = \\\\ 1-11\\times 8 & = \\\\ 1-88 & = \\\\ -87\\end{aligned}\n$$",
